{"context": "published", "host": "www.josephsmithpapers.org", "showHeader": true, "footerStyle": "mini", "statusCode": 200, "uri": "letter-to-newel-knight-and-the-church-in-colesville-28-august-1830", "page": "4", "is404": false, "gallery": [{"image": "/6483/6483_ppallen_128_thumb.jpg", "page": "1", "label": "128", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-newel-knight-and-the-church-in-colesville-28-august-1830/1"}, {"image": "/6483/6483_ppallen_129_thumb.jpg", "page": "2", "label": "129", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-newel-knight-and-the-church-in-colesville-28-august-1830/2"}, {"image": "/6483/6483_ppallen_130_thumb.jpg", "page": "3", "label": "130", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-newel-knight-and-the-church-in-colesville-28-august-1830/3"}, {"image": "/6483/6483_ppallen_131_thumb.jpg", "page": "4", "label": "131", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-newel-knight-and-the-church-in-colesville-28-august-1830/4"}, {"image": "/6483/6483_ppallen_132_thumb.jpg", "page": "5", "label": "132", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-newel-knight-and-the-church-in-colesville-28-august-1830/5"}, {"image": "/6483/6483_ppallen_133_thumb.jpg", "page": "6", "label": "133", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-newel-knight-and-the-church-in-colesville-28-august-1830/6"}, {"image": "/6483/6483_ppallen_134_thumb.jpg", "page": "7", "label": "134", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-newel-knight-and-the-church-in-colesville-28-august-1830/7"}, {"image": "/6483/6483_ppallen_135_thumb.jpg", "page": "8", "label": "135", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-newel-knight-and-the-church-in-colesville-28-august-1830/8"}, {"image": "/6483/6483_ppallen_136_thumb.jpg", "page": "9", "label": "136", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-newel-knight-and-the-church-in-colesville-28-august-1830/9"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "letter-to-newel-knight-and-the-church-in-colesville-28-august-1830", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD1", "documentSeriesTitle": "Letter to Newel Knight and the Church in Colesville, 28 August 1830", "editorialPageNumber": "131", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/26070/26070-0004.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> wolves,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2555762594642993415\"><a href=\"#2555762594642993415\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans8\"><span id=\"documenttrans8\">8</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Matthew 7:15.</p><hr></div></div></aside> therefore we have the more earnest desire to come to see you, but our friends from the west have not yet come,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4988415941889589571\"><a href=\"#4988415941889589571\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans9\"><span id=\"documenttrans9\">9</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">These “friends from the west” probably were <a href=\"/person/david-whitmer\" class=\"referenceInPop\">David Whitmer</a> and <a href=\"/person/hyrum-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Hyrum Smith</a>, who soon after this letter was written arrived from <a href=\"/place/fayette-township-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Fayette</a>, New York (some eighty miles to the northwest), and shortly thereafter transported JS and <a href=\"/person/john-whitmer\" class=\"referenceInPop\">John Whitmer</a> to <a href=\"/place/colesville-township-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Colesville</a>. (JS History, vol. A-1, <a href=\"/paperSummary/history-1838-1856-volume-a-1-23-december-1805-30-august-1834?p=59\" class=\"externalLink\">53</a>.)</p><hr></div></div></aside> and we can get no horse and wagon, and we are not able to come afoot so far, therefore we cannot come this Saturday,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10436365723990820509\"><a href=\"#10436365723990820509\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans10\"><span id=\"documenttrans10\">10</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">28 August 1830. (See postscript to this letter.)</p><hr></div></div></aside> but we look for our friends from the west every day and with safety we can promise to come next Saturday, if the Lord will; therefore our desire is that ye should assemble yourselves together next Saturday [p. 131]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> wolves,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14448369115541427432\"><a href=\"#14448369115541427432\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans8\"><span id=\"documenttrans8\">8</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Matthew 7:15.</p><hr></div></div></aside> therefore we have the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>more earnest desire to come <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>to see you, but our friends <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>from the west have not yet <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>come,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2979657764360187341\"><a href=\"#2979657764360187341\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans9\"><span id=\"documenttrans9\">9</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">These “friends from the west” probably were <a href=\"/person/david-whitmer\" class=\"referenceInPop\">David Whitmer</a> and <a href=\"/person/hyrum-smith\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Hyrum Smith</a>, who soon after this letter was written arrived from <a href=\"/place/fayette-township-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Fayette</a>, New York (some eighty miles to the northwest), and shortly thereafter transported JS and <a href=\"/person/john-whitmer\" class=\"referenceInPop\">John Whitmer</a> to <a href=\"/place/colesville-township-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Colesville</a>. (JS History, vol. A-1, <a href=\"/paperSummary/history-1838-1856-volume-a-1-23-december-1805-30-august-1834?p=59\" class=\"externalLink\">53</a>.)</p><hr></div></div></aside> and we can get no <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>horse and wagon, and we <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>are not able to come afoot <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>so far, therefore we cannot <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>come this Saturday,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"768108382373631662\"><a href=\"#768108382373631662\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans10\"><span id=\"documenttrans10\">10</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">28 August 1830. (See postscript to this letter.)</p><hr></div></div></aside> but we <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>look for our friends from <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the west every day and with <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>safety we can promise to <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>come next Saturday, if the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Lord will; therefore our desire <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>is that ye should assemble <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>yourselves together next Satur